module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.Pullback.IsPullback.Defs
public import Mathlib.Geometry.RingedSpace.LocallyRingedSpace.HasColimits
public import Mathlib.Topology.Category.TopCat.Limits.Pullbacks

/-!
# Pushouts of topological spaces along an injective map, and their open subspaces

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be an *injective* continuous map and `j : Z ⟶ Y` arbitrary, and let

```
Z --i--> X
|        |
j        a
v        v
Y --b--> P
```

be a pushout square of topological spaces.  This file identifies the fibres of the two
canonical maps and deduces that the construction is compatible with restriction to an open
subspace: if `U ⊆ X` and `V ⊆ Y` are open with `i ⁻¹' U = j ⁻¹' V`, then `a '' U ∪ b '' V` is
open in `P`, its preimages under `a` and `b` are exactly `U` and `V`, and the restricted square
is again a pushout.

This is the step which [Stacks Project, Tag 0E25] dismisses with the words "the construction of
the first paragraph is clearly compatible with restriction to compatible open subschemes"; it is
what lets the pushout of a closed immersion and an integral morphism be covered by the affine
models of [Stacks Project, Tag 0ET0].

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutRel` is the equivalence relation on `X ⊕ Y` identifying `i z` with
  `j z`, and `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutQuotient` the resulting quotient space.
* `Stacks.Pushout.restrictOpens` is a continuous map restricted to a pair of opens mapped into
  one another.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_of_isQuotientMap_sum`: a square of topological spaces is a pushout
  square as soon as `b` is injective, the obvious identifications are the only ones, and the
  induced map from `X ⊕ Y` is a quotient map.
* `Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_pushoutQuotient`: the explicit quotient of `X ⊕ Y` is a pushout.
* `Stacks.Pushout.injective_inr_of_isPushout`,
  `Stacks.Pushout.exists_of_inl_eq_inr_of_isPushout`,
  `Stacks.Pushout.eq_or_exists_of_inl_eq_inl_of_isPushout`,
  `Stacks.Pushout.isQuotientMap_sum_of_isPushout`: the four properties above hold in *any*
  pushout square, by comparison with the explicit model.
* `Stacks.Pushout.preimage_inl_image_union_inr_image` and
  `Stacks.Pushout.preimage_inr_image_union_inr_image`: the two preimages of
  `a '' U ∪ b '' V` are `U` and `V`.
* `Stacks.Pushout.isOpen_inl_image_union_inr_image`: that set is open.
* `Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_of_isOpenEmbedding`: the restriction of a pushout square to
  compatible open subspaces is a pushout square, and
  `Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_restrictOpens` is that statement for the subspaces cut out of
  `X`, `Y` and `Z` by an open of the pushout.
* `Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_base_of_isPushout`: a pushout square of locally ringed spaces has a
  pushout square of underlying topological spaces.
* `Stacks.Pushout.exists_opens_preimage_eq_of_isPushout_base`: the compatible pair of opens spans
  an open of the pushout whose two preimages are the given opens.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_of_isQuotientMap_sum` is the mirror image, with the roles of the two
legs exchanged, of a `private` lemma of the same shape in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.FibreProduct.Spectrum`, where it is used to prove Stacks Tag 0B7J.  It
is restated here because that one is not accessible outside its file; the two should be merged
into a single public lemma by a deduplication pass.

The three pointwise properties of a pushout square are obtained by transport along the canonical
isomorphism with the explicit quotient model rather than by analysing
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.colimit_eq` directly: the relation generated by the two
identifications `i z ∼ j z` has to be computed in either case, and computing it on `X ⊕ Y`
involves four cases instead of the nine of the sigma type over `WalkingSpan`.

`Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_of_isOpenEmbedding` takes the restricted square and the four open
embeddings as data, with the compatibilities as hypotheses, rather than forming the subtypes of
the preimages itself.  The reason is that its intended consumers are open subschemes, whose
underlying maps are `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.ι` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.morphismRestrict`, neither of which is syntactically a subtype inclusion; the
two hypotheses `hUa` and `hUb` are exactly the statements proved by
`Stacks.Pushout.preimage_inl_image_union_inr_image` and its companion.
`Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_restrictOpens` records that all nine of its hypotheses are indeed
dischargeable, in the `TopologicalSpace.Opens.inclusion'` spelling that
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrict` uses; the four commuting squares hold by `rfl`
there.

The two closing results reach down from geometry to topology rather than up: the pushout of
schemes of Tag 0E25 is constructed as a pushout of locally ringed spaces, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.forgetToLocallyRingedSpace` does *not* preserve colimits, so a pushout
square of schemes carries no information about its underlying spaces by itself.  That is why
`Stacks.Pushout.exists_opens_preimage_eq_of_isPushout_base` takes the pushout property of the
underlying square as a hypothesis instead of deducing it.

Nothing here carries a Stacks attribute.  The topological statements are a strictly weaker part
of Tag 0E25 — they say nothing about the structure sheaf, and Tag 0B1X is a statement about
pushouts of sets rather than the compatibility with restriction proved here — so claiming either
tag would overstate what is proved, as in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Pushout.ColimitSections`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B1X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B1X)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E25](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E25)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Topology TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Pushout

variable {Z X Y P : TopCat.{u}}

/-! ### A criterion for a square of topological spaces to be a pushout -/

/-- **A pointwise criterion for a pushout of topological spaces.**  The square `i`, `j`, `a`, `b`
is a pushout square as soon as:

* it commutes;
* `b` is injective;
* a point of `X` and a point of `Y` with the same image come from a point of `Z`;
* two points of `X` with the same image are equal or come from two points of `Z` with the same
  image in `Y`;
* the induced map `X ⊕ Y ⟶ P` is a quotient map. -/
theorem isPushout_of_isQuotientMap_sum {i : Z ⟶ X} {j : Z ⟶ Y} {a : X ⟶ P} {b : Y ⟶ P}
    (sq : i ≫ a = j ≫ b) (hb : Function.Injective b)
    (hcross : ∀ (x : X) (y : Y), a x = b y → ∃ z : Z, i z = x ∧ j z = y)
    (hself : ∀ x x' : X, a x = a x' →
      x = x' ∨ ∃ z z' : Z, i z = x ∧ i z' = x' ∧ j z = j z')
    (hq : IsQuotientMap (Sum.elim a b)) : IsPushout i j a b := by
  apply IsPushout.of_isColimit' ⟨sq⟩
  refine PushoutCocone.isColimitAux' _ (fun s ↦ ?_)
  let q : (X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u) → P := Sum.elim a b
  let e : P → (X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u) :=
    (Function.Surjective.hasRightInverse hq.surjective).choose
  have he : Function.RightInverse e q :=
    (Function.Surjective.hasRightInverse hq.surjective).choose_spec
  let d : P → s.pt := Sum.elim s.inl s.inr ∘ e
  have hcond : ∀ z : Z, s.inl (i z) = s.inr (j z) := fun z ↦
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom s.condition z
  have hfiber : ∀ p p', q p = q p' → Sum.elim s.inl s.inr p = Sum.elim s.inl s.inr p' := by
    rintro (x | y) (x' | y') h
    · rcases hself x x' h with rfl | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
      · rfl
      · calc
          s.inl x = s.inl (i z) := by rw [hz]
          _ = s.inr (j z) := hcond z
          _ = s.inr (j z') := by rw [hj]
          _ = s.inl (i z') := (hcond z').symm
          _ = s.inl x' := by rw [hz']
    · obtain ⟨z, hz, hj⟩ := hcross x y' h
      calc
        s.inl x = s.inl (i z) := by rw [hz]
        _ = s.inr (j z) := hcond z
        _ = s.inr y' := by rw [hj]
    · obtain ⟨z, hz, hj⟩ := hcross x' y h.symm
      calc
        s.inr y = s.inr (j z) := by rw [hj]
        _ = s.inl (i z) := (hcond z).symm
        _ = s.inl x' := by rw [hz]
    · exact congrArg s.inr (hb h)
  have hdq : d ∘ q = Sum.elim s.inl s.inr := funext fun p ↦ hfiber _ _ (he (q p))
  refine ⟨TopCat.ofHom ⟨d, hq.continuous_iff.mpr ?_⟩, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [hdq]
    exact Continuous.sumElim s.inl.hom.continuous s.inr.hom.continuous
  · exact ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun x ↦ congrFun hdq (.inl x)
  · exact ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun y ↦ congrFun hdq (.inr y)
  · intro m hm hn
    refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun p ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := hq.surjective p
    rcases p with x | y
    · exact (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hm x).trans (congrFun hdq (.inl x)).symm
    · exact (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hn y).trans (congrFun hdq (.inr y)).symm

/-! ### The explicit quotient model -/

/-- The relation on `X ⊕ Y` identifying `i z` with `j z` for every `z : Z`.  When `i` is
injective it is an equivalence relation, `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutSetoid`. -/
def pushoutRel (i : Z ⟶ X) (j : Z ⟶ Y) : (X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u) → (X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u) →
    Prop
  | .inl x, .inl x' => x = x' ∨ ∃ z z' : Z, i z = x ∧ i z' = x' ∧ j z = j z'
  | .inl x, .inr y => ∃ z : Z, i z = x ∧ j z = y
  | .inr y, .inl x => ∃ z : Z, i z = x ∧ j z = y
  | .inr y, .inr y' => y = y'

variable (i : Z ⟶ X) (j : Z ⟶ Y)

/-- `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutRel` is reflexive. -/
lemma pushoutRel_refl (p : (X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u)) : pushoutRel i j p p := by
  cases p with
  | inl x => exact Or.inl rfl
  | inr y => exact rfl

/-- `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutRel` is symmetric. -/
lemma pushoutRel_symm {p p' : (X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u)} (h : pushoutRel i j p p') :
    pushoutRel i j p' p := by
  rcases p with x | y <;> rcases p' with x' | y'
  · rcases h with rfl | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
    · exact Or.inl rfl
    · exact Or.inr ⟨z', z, hz', hz, hj.symm⟩
  · exact h
  · exact h
  · exact h.symm

/-- `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutRel` is transitive when `i` is injective.  Injectivity is what makes
the composite of `i z ∼ j z` and `j z' ∼ i z'` identify `i z` with `i z'` only when the two
points of `Z` already have the same image in `Y`. -/
lemma pushoutRel_trans (hi : Function.Injective i)
    {p p' p'' : (X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u)} (h₁ : pushoutRel i j p p')
    (h₂ : pushoutRel i j p' p'') : pushoutRel i j p p'' := by
  rcases p with x | y <;> rcases p' with x' | y' <;> rcases p'' with x'' | y''
  · rcases h₁ with rfl | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
    · exact h₂
    · rcases h₂ with rfl | ⟨w, w', hw, hw', hjw⟩
      · exact Or.inr ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
      · obtain rfl : z' = w := hi (hz'.trans hw.symm)
        exact Or.inr ⟨z, w', hz, hw', hj.trans hjw⟩
  · rcases h₁ with rfl | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
    · exact h₂
    · obtain ⟨w, hw, hwj⟩ := h₂
      obtain rfl : z' = w := hi (hz'.trans hw.symm)
      exact ⟨z, hz, hj.trans hwj⟩
  · obtain ⟨z, hz, hzj⟩ := h₁
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hwj⟩ := h₂
    exact Or.inr ⟨z, w, hz, hw, hzj.trans hwj.symm⟩
  · exact h₂ ▸ h₁
  · obtain ⟨z, hz, hzj⟩ := h₁
    rcases h₂ with rfl | ⟨w, w', hw, hw', hjw⟩
    · exact ⟨z, hz, hzj⟩
    · obtain rfl : z = w := hi (hz.trans hw.symm)
      exact ⟨w', hw', hjw.symm.trans hzj⟩
  · obtain ⟨z, hz, hzj⟩ := h₁
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hwj⟩ := h₂
    obtain rfl : z = w := hi (hz.trans hw.symm)
    exact hzj.symm.trans hwj
  · exact h₁ ▸ h₂
  · exact h₁.trans h₂

/-- The equivalence relation on `X ⊕ Y` generated by `i z ∼ j z`, for an injective `i`. -/
def pushoutSetoid (hi : Function.Injective i) : Setoid ((X : Type u) ⊕ (Y : Type u)) where
  r := pushoutRel i j
  iseqv := ⟨pushoutRel_refl i j, pushoutRel_symm i j, pushoutRel_trans i j hi⟩

/-- The pushout of `X ← Z → Y` in topological spaces, realized as the quotient of `X ⊕ Y` by
`Stacks.Pushout.pushoutSetoid`. -/
def pushoutQuotient (hi : Function.Injective i) : TopCat.{u} :=
  TopCat.of (Quotient (pushoutSetoid i j hi))

/-- The canonical map from `X` to `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutQuotient`. -/
def pushoutQuotientInl (hi : Function.Injective i) : X ⟶ pushoutQuotient i j hi :=
  TopCat.ofHom ⟨fun x ↦ Quotient.mk _ (.inl x), continuous_quotient_mk'.comp continuous_inl⟩

/-- The canonical map from `Y` to `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutQuotient`. -/
def pushoutQuotientInr (hi : Function.Injective i) : Y ⟶ pushoutQuotient i j hi :=
  TopCat.ofHom ⟨fun y ↦ Quotient.mk _ (.inr y), continuous_quotient_mk'.comp continuous_inr⟩

variable (hi : Function.Injective i)

/-- The map `X ⊕ Y ⟶ Stacks.Pushout.pushoutQuotient` induced by the two canonical maps is the
quotient map. -/
lemma sum_elim_pushoutQuotient :
    Sum.elim (pushoutQuotientInl i j hi) (pushoutQuotientInr i j hi) =
      Quotient.mk (pushoutSetoid i j hi) := by
  funext p
  rcases p with x | y <;> rfl

/-- **The explicit quotient of `X ⊕ Y` is a pushout.** -/
theorem isPushout_pushoutQuotient :
    IsPushout i j (pushoutQuotientInl i j hi) (pushoutQuotientInr i j hi) := by
  refine isPushout_of_isQuotientMap_sum ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun z ↦ ?_
    rw [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply]
    exact Quotient.sound ⟨z, rfl, rfl⟩
  · intro y y' h
    exact Quotient.exact h
  · intro x y h
    obtain ⟨z, hz, hj⟩ := Quotient.exact h
    exact ⟨z, hz, hj⟩
  · intro x x' h
    rcases Quotient.exact h with rfl | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
    · exact Or.inl rfl
    · exact Or.inr ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
  · rw [sum_elim_pushoutQuotient]
    exact isQuotientMap_quotient_mk'

/-- The image under `u` of a preimage under `a'` is the preimage under `a` of the image under
`w`, when `w` is injective, the square commutes and `a x ∈ range w` forces `x ∈ range u`. -/
private theorem image_preimage_eq_preimage_image' {X' P' X P : Type*} {u : X' → X}
    {a' : X' → P'} {a : X → P} {w : P' → P} (hw : Function.Injective w)
    (ea : ∀ x', w (a' x') = a (u x'))
    (hua : ∀ x, a x ∈ Set.range w → x ∈ Set.range u) (S : Set P') :
    u '' (a' ⁻¹' S) = a ⁻¹' (w '' S) := by
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨x', hx', rfl⟩
    exact ⟨a' x', hx', ea x'⟩
  · rintro x ⟨s, hs, hsx⟩
    obtain ⟨x', rfl⟩ := hua x ⟨s, hsx⟩
    exact ⟨x', by rwa [Set.mem_preimage, hw ((ea x').trans hsx.symm)], rfl⟩

/-! ### The same properties in an arbitrary pushout square -/

section

variable {a : X ⟶ P} {b : Y ⟶ P} (h : IsPushout i j a b)

include h hi

/-- Any pushout square along an injective map is, as a topological space, the explicit quotient
of `X ⊕ Y` of `Stacks.Pushout.pushoutQuotient`, compatibly with the two canonical maps. -/
lemma exists_homeomorph_pushoutQuotient :
    ∃ e : (pushoutQuotient i j hi : Type u) ≃ₜ P,
      (∀ x : X, e (pushoutQuotientInl i j hi x) = a x) ∧
      (∀ y : Y, e (pushoutQuotientInr i j hi y) = b y) := by
  let E := (isPushout_pushoutQuotient i j hi).isoIsPushout X Y h
  refine ⟨TopCat.homeoOfIso E, fun x ↦ ?_, fun y ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact (ConcreteCategory.comp_apply _ E.hom x).symm.trans
      (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
        (IsPushout.inl_isoIsPushout_hom X Y (isPushout_pushoutQuotient i j hi) h) x)
  · exact (ConcreteCategory.comp_apply _ E.hom y).symm.trans
      (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
        (IsPushout.inr_isoIsPushout_hom X Y (isPushout_pushoutQuotient i j hi) h) y)

/-- **In a pushout square along an injective map, the other leg is injective.** -/
theorem injective_inr_of_isPushout : Function.Injective b := by
  obtain ⟨e, -, hr⟩ := exists_homeomorph_pushoutQuotient i j hi h
  intro y y' hyy
  have hq : pushoutQuotientInr i j hi y = pushoutQuotientInr i j hi y' :=
    e.injective ((hr y).trans (hyy.trans (hr y').symm))
  exact Quotient.exact hq

/-- **A point of `X` and a point of `Y` with the same image in a pushout come from `Z`.** -/
theorem exists_of_inl_eq_inr_of_isPushout (x : X) (y : Y) (hxy : a x = b y) :
    ∃ z : Z, i z = x ∧ j z = y := by
  obtain ⟨e, hl, hr⟩ := exists_homeomorph_pushoutQuotient i j hi h
  have : pushoutQuotientInl i j hi x = pushoutQuotientInr i j hi y :=
    e.injective ((hl x).trans (hxy.trans (hr y).symm))
  obtain ⟨z, hz, hj⟩ := Quotient.exact this
  exact ⟨z, hz, hj⟩

/-- **Two points of `X` with the same image in a pushout.**  They are equal, or they are the
images of two points of `Z` with the same image in `Y`. -/
theorem eq_or_exists_of_inl_eq_inl_of_isPushout (x x' : X) (hxx : a x = a x') :
    x = x' ∨ ∃ z z' : Z, i z = x ∧ i z' = x' ∧ j z = j z' := by
  obtain ⟨e, hl, -⟩ := exists_homeomorph_pushoutQuotient i j hi h
  have : pushoutQuotientInl i j hi x = pushoutQuotientInl i j hi x' :=
    e.injective ((hl x).trans (hxx.trans (hl x').symm))
  rcases Quotient.exact this with hEq | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
  · exact Or.inl hEq
  · exact Or.inr ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩

/-- **The two legs of a pushout of topological spaces form a quotient map.** -/
theorem isQuotientMap_sum_of_isPushout : IsQuotientMap (Sum.elim a b) := by
  obtain ⟨e, hl, hr⟩ := exists_homeomorph_pushoutQuotient i j hi h
  have hfun : ∀ p, (e ∘ Quotient.mk (pushoutSetoid i j hi)) p = Sum.elim a b p := by
    rintro (x | y)
    · exact hl x
    · exact hr y
  exact funext hfun ▸ e.isQuotientMap.comp isQuotientMap_quotient_mk'

/-! ### Compatible opens -/

section

variable {U : Set X} {V : Set Y} (hUV : i ⁻¹' U = j ⁻¹' V)

include hUV

/-- **The preimage in `X` of a compatible pair of opens.**  If `i ⁻¹' U = j ⁻¹' V`, then `U` is
exactly the preimage under `a` of the set `a '' U ∪ b '' V`. -/
theorem preimage_inl_image_union_inr_image : a ⁻¹' (a '' U ∪ b '' V) = U := by
  have key : ∀ z : Z, i z ∈ U ↔ j z ∈ V := fun z ↦ Set.ext_iff.mp hUV z
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ (fun x hx ↦ Or.inl ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩)
  rintro x (⟨x', hx', hxx⟩ | ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩)
  · rcases eq_or_exists_of_inl_eq_inl_of_isPushout i j hi h x x' hxx.symm with
      rfl | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
    · exact hx'
    · refine hz ▸ (key z).mpr ?_
      exact hj ▸ (key z').mp (hz' ▸ hx')
  · obtain ⟨z, hz, hj⟩ := exists_of_inl_eq_inr_of_isPushout i j hi h x y hxy.symm
    exact hz ▸ (key z).mpr (hj ▸ hy)

/-- **The preimage in `Y` of a compatible pair of opens.**  If `i ⁻¹' U = j ⁻¹' V`, then `V` is
exactly the preimage under `b` of the set `a '' U ∪ b '' V`. -/
theorem preimage_inr_image_union_inr_image : b ⁻¹' (a '' U ∪ b '' V) = V := by
  have key : ∀ z : Z, i z ∈ U ↔ j z ∈ V := fun z ↦ Set.ext_iff.mp hUV z
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ (fun y hy ↦ Or.inr ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩)
  rintro y (⟨x, hx, hxy⟩ | ⟨y', hy', hyy⟩)
  · obtain ⟨z, hz, hj⟩ := exists_of_inl_eq_inr_of_isPushout i j hi h x y hxy
    exact hj ▸ (key z).mp (hz ▸ hx)
  · exact injective_inr_of_isPushout i j hi h hyy ▸ hy'

/-- **A compatible pair of opens spans an open of the pushout.** -/
theorem isOpen_inl_image_union_inr_image (hU : IsOpen U) (hV : IsOpen V) :
    IsOpen (a '' U ∪ b '' V) := by
  rw [← (isQuotientMap_sum_of_isPushout i j hi h).isCoinducing.isOpen_preimage]
  refine isOpen_sum_iff.mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · change IsOpen (a ⁻¹' (a '' U ∪ b '' V))
    rw [preimage_inl_image_union_inr_image i j hi h hUV]
    exact hU
  · change IsOpen (b ⁻¹' (a '' U ∪ b '' V))
    rw [preimage_inr_image_union_inr_image i j hi h hUV]
    exact hV

end

/-! ### Restriction to an open subspace -/

/-- **The restriction of a pushout square of topological spaces to open subspaces.**  Let
`i`, `j`, `a`, `b` be a pushout square with `i` injective, and let `t`, `u`, `v`, `w` be open
embeddings of a second square into it, commuting with all four maps.  If moreover the images of
`u` and `v` are exactly the preimages under `a` and `b` of the image of `w`, and the image of `t`
is the preimage under `i` of the image of `u`, then the second square is again a pushout square.

The hypotheses `hua` and `hvb` are supplied by
`Stacks.Pushout.preimage_inl_image_union_inr_image` and
`Stacks.Pushout.preimage_inr_image_union_inr_image` when `w` is the inclusion of the open
spanned by a compatible pair of opens. -/
theorem isPushout_of_isOpenEmbedding {Z' X' Y' P' : TopCat.{u}} {i' : Z' ⟶ X'} {j' : Z' ⟶ Y'}
    {a' : X' ⟶ P'} {b' : Y' ⟶ P'} {t : Z' ⟶ Z} {u : X' ⟶ X} {v : Y' ⟶ Y} {w : P' ⟶ P}
    (hu : IsOpenEmbedding u) (hv : IsOpenEmbedding v) (hw : IsOpenEmbedding w)
    (sqi : i' ≫ u = t ≫ i) (sqj : j' ≫ v = t ≫ j)
    (sqa : a' ≫ w = u ≫ a) (sqb : b' ≫ w = v ≫ b)
    (hua : ∀ x : X, a x ∈ Set.range w → x ∈ Set.range u)
    (hvb : ∀ y : Y, b y ∈ Set.range w → y ∈ Set.range v)
    (hti : ∀ z : Z, i z ∈ Set.range u → z ∈ Set.range t) :
    IsPushout i' j' a' b' := by
  have ei : ∀ z' : Z', u (i' z') = i (t z') := fun z' ↦ ConcreteCategory.congr_hom sqi z'
  have ej : ∀ z' : Z', v (j' z') = j (t z') := fun z' ↦ ConcreteCategory.congr_hom sqj z'
  have ea : ∀ x' : X', w (a' x') = a (u x') := fun x' ↦ ConcreteCategory.congr_hom sqa x'
  have eb : ∀ y' : Y', w (b' y') = b (v y') := fun y' ↦ ConcreteCategory.congr_hom sqb y'
  have ew : ∀ z : Z, a (i z) = b (j z) := fun z ↦ ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h.w z
  have himu := image_preimage_eq_preimage_image' (u := u) (a' := a') (a := a)
    hw.injective ea hua
  have himv := image_preimage_eq_preimage_image' (u := v) (a' := b') (a := b)
    hw.injective eb hvb
  have hqg := isQuotientMap_sum_of_isPushout i j hi h
  refine isPushout_of_isQuotientMap_sum ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun z' ↦ ?_
    rw [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply]
    refine hw.injective ?_
    rw [ea, eb, ei, ej]
    exact ew (t z')
  · intro y₁ y₂ hy
    refine hv.injective ?_
    refine injective_inr_of_isPushout i j hi h ?_
    rw [← eb, ← eb, hy]
  · intro x' y' hxy
    have hab : a (u x') = b (v y') := by rw [← ea, ← eb, hxy]
    obtain ⟨z, hz, hj⟩ := exists_of_inl_eq_inr_of_isPushout i j hi h _ _ hab
    obtain ⟨z', rfl⟩ := hti z (hz ▸ ⟨x', rfl⟩)
    exact ⟨z', hu.injective ((ei z').trans hz), hv.injective ((ej z').trans hj)⟩
  · intro x₁ x₂ hx
    have hab : a (u x₁) = a (u x₂) := by rw [← ea, ← ea, hx]
    rcases eq_or_exists_of_inl_eq_inl_of_isPushout i j hi h _ _ hab with
      heq | ⟨z, z', hz, hz', hj⟩
    · exact Or.inl (hu.injective heq)
    · obtain ⟨z₁, rfl⟩ := hti z (hz ▸ ⟨x₁, rfl⟩)
      obtain ⟨z₂, rfl⟩ := hti z' (hz' ▸ ⟨x₂, rfl⟩)
      refine Or.inr ⟨z₁, z₂, hu.injective ((ei z₁).trans hz),
        hu.injective ((ei z₂).trans hz'), hv.injective ?_⟩
      rw [ej, ej]
      exact hj
  · refine (isQuotientMap_iff _).mpr ⟨Topology.IsCoinducing.of_isOpen_preimage_iff_isOpen
      fun S ↦ ?_, fun p' ↦ ?_⟩
    · rw [isOpen_sum_iff]
      rw [show Sum.inl ⁻¹' (Sum.elim a' b' ⁻¹' S) = a' ⁻¹' S from rfl,
        show Sum.inr ⁻¹' (Sum.elim a' b' ⁻¹' S) = b' ⁻¹' S from rfl,
        hu.isOpen_iff_image_isOpen (s := a' ⁻¹' S),
        hv.isOpen_iff_image_isOpen (s := b' ⁻¹' S), himu, himv,
        hw.isOpen_iff_image_isOpen (s := S), ← hqg.isCoinducing.isOpen_preimage,
        isOpen_sum_iff]
      exact Iff.rfl
    · obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := hqg.surjective (w p')
      rcases q with x | y
      · obtain ⟨x', rfl⟩ := hua x ⟨p', hq.symm⟩
        exact ⟨.inl x', hw.injective ((ea x').trans hq)⟩
      · obtain ⟨y', rfl⟩ := hvb y ⟨p', hq.symm⟩
        exact ⟨.inr y', hw.injective ((eb y').trans hq)⟩

end

/-- A continuous map restricted to a pair of opens, one in the source and one in the target,
mapped into one another.  The objects are spelled with
`TopologicalSpace.Opens.toTopCat`, as in `AlgebraicGeometry.PresheafedSpace.restrict`. -/
def restrictOpens {A B : TopCat.{u}} (f : A ⟶ B) (S : Opens A) (T : Opens B)
    (hST : ∀ x : A, x ∈ S → f x ∈ T) :
    (Opens.toTopCat A).obj S ⟶ (Opens.toTopCat B).obj T :=
  TopCat.ofHom ⟨fun x ↦ ⟨f x.1, hST x.1 x.2⟩,
    Continuous.subtype_mk (f.hom.continuous.comp continuous_subtype_val) _⟩

/-- **The restriction of a pushout square of topological spaces to the subspaces cut out by an
open of the pushout.**  This is `Stacks.Pushout.isPushout_of_isOpenEmbedding` applied to the four
inclusions `TopologicalSpace.Opens.inclusion'`, which is the spelling in which
`AlgebraicGeometry.PresheafedSpace.restrict` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrict` take their open embeddings. -/
theorem isPushout_restrictOpens {a : X ⟶ P} {b : Y ⟶ P} (h : IsPushout i j a b)
    (hi : Function.Injective i) (W : Opens P) :
    IsPushout
      (restrictOpens i ((Opens.map (i ≫ a)).obj W) ((Opens.map a).obj W) fun _ hz ↦ hz)
      (restrictOpens j ((Opens.map (i ≫ a)).obj W) ((Opens.map b).obj W) fun z hz ↦ by
        have hzW : a (i z) ∈ W := hz
        rwa [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, h.w, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] at hzW)
      (restrictOpens a ((Opens.map a).obj W) W fun _ hx ↦ hx)
      (restrictOpens b ((Opens.map b).obj W) W fun _ hy ↦ hy) := by
  refine isPushout_of_isOpenEmbedding i j hi h (u := Opens.inclusion' _)
    (v := Opens.inclusion' _) (w := Opens.inclusion' W) (t := Opens.inclusion' _)
    (Opens.isOpenEmbedding _) (Opens.isOpenEmbedding _) (Opens.isOpenEmbedding W)
    rfl rfl rfl rfl (fun _ h ↦ ?_) (fun _ h ↦ ?_) (fun _ h ↦ ?_) <;>
    rw [Opens.set_range_inclusion'] at h ⊢ <;> exact h

/-! ### From locally ringed spaces and schemes down to topological spaces -/

/-- **A pushout of locally ringed spaces is a pushout of the underlying topological spaces.**
The underlying-space functor is the composite of
`LocallyRingedSpace.forgetToSheafedSpace` and
`SheafedSpace.forget`, both of which preserve colimits. -/
theorem isPushout_base_of_isPushout {Z X Y P : LocallyRingedSpace.{u}}
    {i : Z ⟶ X} {j : Z ⟶ Y} {a : X ⟶ P} {b : Y ⟶ P} (h : IsPushout i j a b) :
    IsPushout i.base j.base a.base b.base :=
  h.map (LocallyRingedSpace.forgetToSheafedSpace ⋙
    SheafedSpace.forget CommRingCat)

/-- **The open of a pushout spanned by a compatible pair of opens.**  Let `i`, `j`, `a`, `b` be a
square of schemes whose underlying square of topological spaces is a pushout square, with `i`
injective on points, and let `U` and `V` be opens of `X` and `Y` with `i ⁻¹ᵁ U = j ⁻¹ᵁ V`.  Then
the union of the images of `U` and `V` is an open `W` of `P` with `a ⁻¹ᵁ W = U` and
`b ⁻¹ᵁ W = V`.

This is the shape in which the construction of [Stacks Project, Tag 0E25] produces its affine
charts: the hypothesis on `U` and `V` is the conclusion of [Stacks Project, Tag 0ECJ], namely
`Stacks.Pushout.exists_affineOpens_preimage_eq`. -/
theorem exists_opens_preimage_eq_of_isPushout_base {Z X Y P : Scheme.{u}}
    {i : Z ⟶ X} {j : Z ⟶ Y} {a : X ⟶ P} {b : Y ⟶ P}
    (hbase : IsPushout i.base j.base a.base b.base) (hi : Function.Injective i.base)
    (U : X.Opens) (V : Y.Opens) (hUV : i ⁻¹ᵁ U = j ⁻¹ᵁ V) :
    ∃ W : P.Opens, (W : Set P) = a.base '' (U : Set X) ∪ b.base '' (V : Set Y) ∧
      a ⁻¹ᵁ W = U ∧ b ⁻¹ᵁ W = V := by
  have hUV' : i.base ⁻¹' (U : Set X) = j.base ⁻¹' (V : Set Y) :=
    congrArg (fun O : Z.Opens ↦ (O : Set Z)) hUV
  refine ⟨⟨_, isOpen_inl_image_union_inr_image i.base j.base hi hbase hUV' U.2 V.2⟩, rfl,
    TopologicalSpace.Opens.ext ?_, TopologicalSpace.Opens.ext ?_⟩
  · exact preimage_inl_image_union_inr_image i.base j.base hi hbase hUV'
  · exact preimage_inr_image_union_inr_image i.base j.base hi hbase hUV'

end Stacks.Pushout

